  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mongolia: Child Protection and Enhancement Project (CPEP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To strengthen the capacity of Legal Committees for Child Rights (LCCRs) to effectively manage cases of children in contact with the law. 2) To increase the ability of civil society organizations (CSOs) to rehabilitate and reintegrate children released from correction centres into society in piloted rural and peri-urban areas. 3) To improve the knowledge of Internet safety and netiquette by children.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Authority of Family, Child, and Youth Development (AFCYD), Secretariats for the LCCRs, CSOs, and children, particularly those in remote aimags and soums.Indirect beneficiaries: Vulnerable children, families, and communities in Mongolia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to ensure that children in Mongolia are supported by an enhanced child protection system.</narrative>
  </description>
